  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Discretionary Funding - Rights in Crisis (RiC) Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.  Local humanitarian leadership through thoughtful and context based capability development initiatives in the areas of emergency preparedness and response, adherence to core humanitarian standards and the ability to inform and influence relevant humanitarian within the humanitarian system in the Philippines. Work with government, the United Nation (UN) Humanitarian Country Team (HCT), private sector and other humanitarian stakeholders to support the review, revision and finalization of consensus -driven scenarios (which includes the anticipated 7.2 magnitude earthquake) and consequent country contingency plans. Within these plans identify implications for Oxfam and its strategic humanitarian Partners and ensure relevant and appropriate preparedness and response capabilities are in place. 2.  Support the idealisation, innovation, refinement and implementation of impactful humanitarian approaches and solutions especially with the START network and the DEPP initiatives to localize humanitarian preparedness and response to communities and households, with an emphasis on the most vulnerable.  3.  Influence national and local policies, especially in the aftermath of a natural disaster or conflict, to ensure rights realization of affected communities in long -term recovery and resilience within rehabilitation, reconstruction and development plans. 4.  Support strategic humanitarian and adaptation and risk reduction (ARR) partners and networks&apos; influencing of regional and national adaptation and risk reduction platforms to strengthen Philippine disaster management law, structures and mechanisms at the national and local levels.</narrative>
  </description>
